                <pb facs="cr_d14-1" n="1" xml:id="cr_d14-1"/>

                <head>CR–14. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The International Bank for Reconstruction and Development authorized the
                    following loans to Costa Rica during the years 1958–1960: (1) $3.5 million to
                    the Central Bank of Costa Rica on February 11, 1959, to relend for agricultural
                    and light industrial development. (2) $2 million to the Central Bank of Costa
                    Rica on May 4, 1960, to finance loans to industrial firms for importing capital
                    goods. (International Bank for Reconstruction and Development, <pb facs="0512"
                        n="424" type="typeset" xml:id="pg424"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Fourteenth Annua1 Report, 1958–1959</hi>, page 30; and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Fifteenth Annual Report, 1959–1960</hi>, page
                    32)</p>
                <p>The Export-Import Bank authorized a credit of $3 million to Costa Rica on April
                    15, 1960 for Inter-American Highway construction, but no funds were disbursed in
                    1960. For additional information, see Export-Import Bank of Washington, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Report to the Congress for the Twelve Months Ending June
                        30, 1961</hi>, page 144.</p>
            </div>
